[center][size=6][b]ARPG MOVEMENT[/b][/size]
[size=4]Click. Hold. Explore.[/size]

[b]Turn Fields of Mistria into a more direct, mouse-driven adventure.[/b]
Move with intention, interact from a distance, and let the right tool snap into your hand when you need it.
[/center]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/phob/mistria-fluid/main/nexus/assets/floral-vine-separator.png[/img][/center]

[size=5][b]YOUR NEW MOVEMENT KIT[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]AUTO TOOL SWAPPING[/b] — Click a rock, tree, stump, dig spot, dry crop, tillable patch, bug, breakable, or fishable water and the right tool or weapon is equipped before your character acts.[/*]
[*][b]CURSOR AIMING[/b] — Swings, casts, and tool reach follow your cursor, swing after swing, even while you are walking.[/*]
[*][b]SMART INTERACTIONS[/b] — Click a distant NPC, chest, door, or usable object to walk into range and interact.[/*]
[*][b]MOUSE-DRIVEN MOVEMENT[/b] — Hold right mouse to steer; tap right mouse to path to a destination.[/*]
[*][b]MOUNTED & SWIMMING CONTROLS[/b] — Keep steering while riding or swimming, and tap a destination to ride there.[/*]
[*][b]CLICK-AWAY MENUS[/b] — Left- or right-click outside a normal menu to close it; dialogue and confirmation prompts stay protected.[/*]
[*][b]CLEAR CLICK FEEDBACK[/b] — A normal poof confirms a valid destination; a red poof means it cannot be reached, including spots that would need a walk across open water.[/*]
[/list]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/phob/mistria-fluid/main/nexus/assets/floral-vine-separator.png[/img][/center]

[size=5][b]CONTROLS[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Hold right mouse[/b] — Steer toward the cursor. Move close to walk; move farther away to run. Hold your normal Walk control whenever you want to stay at walking pace.[/*]
[*][b]Tap right mouse on the ground[/b] — Move to that spot automatically, navigating around obstacles. Mounted routes stay outdoors in the current room, never cross open water, and stop instead of jumping.[/*]
[*][b]Tap right mouse on a character or object[/b] — Walk into range and interact. Nearby taps still behave like the normal Interact button.[/*]
[*][b]WASD / jump / tool / E / Esc[/b] — Instantly cancel mouse-driven movement. Keyboard control always wins.[/*]
[/list]

While right mouse is held, Interact is temporarily suppressed so you can steer past people, chests, and doors without activating them.

Mounted click-to-move keeps the game's normal riding movement, collision, speed, animation, footsteps, perks, and rendering. It cancels on dismount, mount blockers, room changes, movement keys, or actions. If an NPC or animal blocks the route for too long, the mod replans twice and then stops.

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/phob/mistria-fluid/main/nexus/assets/floral-vine-separator.png[/img][/center]

[size=5][b]AUTO TOOL SWAPPING[/b][/size]

Enabled by default and built around your usual left-click tool action:

[list]
[*]Click a [b]rock[/b] to equip a pickaxe.[/*]
[*]Click a [b]wild tree or stump[/b] to equip an axe. Player-planted saplings and trees keep your current selection, protecting them from an accidental automatic axe swap.[/*]
[*]Click a [b]dig spot[/b] to equip a shovel.[/*]
[*]Click a [b]barrel, crate, or debris pile[/b] in the mines — or a branch or leaf pile on the farm — to draw your weapon.[/*]
[*]Click a [b]thirsty crop[/b] to equip the watering can, a [b]tillable patch[/b] to equip the hoe, or a [b]bug[/b] to equip the net — whenever the game itself says that tool would act there.[/*]
[*]Click [b]fishable water[/b] to equip the fishing rod.[/*]
[*]In the [b]mines[/b], your weapon is drawn the moment a monster is close to you or under your cursor — combat always outranks tools.[/*]
[/list]

The mod searches your whole inventory and changes toolbar pages when needed. It will not equip a tool that is too weak or missing. A fresh click on a recognized object can still arm the correct tool just outside its reach, so you can step closer and swing again. Anything the item already in your hand can do where you clicked is left alone, so seeds, placements, player-planted trees, and the tool you deliberately picked are never swapped away. Manually selecting an axe still lets you chop a planted tree.

Press [b]F6[/b] to toggle Auto Tool Swapping. Your choice is remembered, and the key can be changed with the [b]auto_select_hotkey[/b] setting.

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/phob/mistria-fluid/main/nexus/assets/floral-vine-separator.png[/img][/center]

[size=5][b]CURSOR AIMING[/b][/size]

Clicking with a weapon or tool turns your character toward the cursor before the action starts, so swings, casts, and tool reach go where you are pointing instead of wherever you last walked. Hold the button down and every repeat swing re-aims at the cursor.

Tall objects are handled too: clicking the overhanging top of a rock or tree re-aims the strike at the object you actually clicked, instead of whiffing at the empty tile behind it.

Action clicks also keep aiming at the cursor while you walk, instead of snapping to your direction of travel. Movement still wins when you want it to: a movement key or a steering hold sets your facing exactly as it does in vanilla.

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/phob/mistria-fluid/main/nexus/assets/floral-vine-separator.png[/img][/center]

[size=5][b]INSTALLATION[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fieldsofmistria/mods/78][b]MOMI 0.15.2 or newer[/b][/url].[/*]
[*]Close Fields of Mistria.[/*]
[*]Open the game's installation folder. The default Steam location on Windows is [b]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Fields of Mistria[/b].[/*]
[*]If you installed Steam or the game somewhere else, open your Steam Library, right-click [b]Fields of Mistria[/b], and choose [b]Manage → Browse local files[/b].[/*]
[*]Inside the Fields of Mistria folder, create a folder named [b]mods[/b] if it does not already exist.[/*]
[*]Extract the downloaded mod archive into that [b]mods[/b] folder.[/*]
[*]Check that the final file path is [b]Fields of Mistria\mods\arpg_movement\manifest.json[/b]. If you see an extra nested [b]arpg_movement[/b] folder, move the inner folder up one level.[/*]
[*]Run MOMI and install your mods.[/*]
[/list]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/phob/mistria-fluid/main/nexus/assets/floral-vine-separator.png[/img][/center]

[size=5][b]CONFIGURATION[/b][/size]

Open [b]Journal → Settings → ARPG Movement[/b] to change gameplay options in game. Changes save immediately to [b]%LOCALAPPDATA%\FieldsOfMistria\mod_data\arpg_movement\arpg_movement.json[/b].

[list]
[*][b]enabled[/b] — Enable or disable the mod without uninstalling it.[/*]
[*][b]hold_to_steer[/b] — Toggle steering with a held right mouse button.[/*]
[*][b]tap_to_pathfind[/b] — Toggle moving to a tapped destination, including while mounted.[/*]
[*][b]mouse_move_mounted_only[/b] — Limit mouse movement to horseback. On foot, right mouse then behaves exactly like vanilla.[/*]
[*][b]tap_seconds[/b] and [b]steer_start_seconds[/b] — Adjust tap and steering timing.[/*]
[*][b]walk_within_px[/b], [b]run_beyond_px[/b], and [b]stop_within_px[/b] — Tune the stop/walk/run distance bands around the cursor.[/*]
[*][b]click_to_interact[/b] — Toggle automatic approach and interaction.[/*]
[*][b]interact_radius_px[/b] — How close a tapped object must be to trigger a direct interaction instead of walking there first.[/*]
[*][b]click_marker[/b] and [b]invalid_click_marker[/b] — Toggle destination feedback.[/*]
[*][b]auto_select_action_item[/b] — Toggle Auto Tool Swapping.[/*]
[*][b]auto_select_hotkey[/b] — The key that toggles Auto Tool Swapping in game. Default [b]"F6"[/b]; combinations like [b]"SHIFT+F6"[/b] and gamepad buttons like [b]"GAMEPAD_Y"[/b] also work. All valid key names are listed in the [url=https://github.com/Garethp/Mods-of-Mistria-Installer/blob/main/docs/MMAPI/API_REFERENCE.md#hotkey]MMAPI hotkey documentation[/url]; a name it does not recognize falls back to F6.[/*]
[*][b]face_cursor_on_action[/b] — Toggle turning toward the cursor when you act.[/*]
[*][b]cursor_targeting_on_action[/b] — Toggle cursor aiming for action clicks made while walking.[/*]
[*][b]click_outside_closes_menus[/b] — Toggle closing menus by clicking outside them.[/*]
[*][b]sword_enemy_range_px[/b] — How close a monster must be for a mine click to draw your weapon (clicks directly at a monster always do).[/*]
[/list]
